# The build context is nothing but what the release build needs. A working checkout can hold tens of GB of build output
# and caches (`target/`, `refs/`, `.venv`, `node_modules`), so the rule is: leave everything out, then let these in.
# A new top-level directory is therefore never sent by accident.
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!crates
!.git
!LICENSE-MIT
!LICENSE-APACHE
!NOTICE
!THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md
!LICENSES
# inside what is let in
**/target
**/node_modules
**/__pycache__
